### RBAC role families demo: one working request per endpoint, plus the scenarios that matter.
### Works with the VS Code REST Client and the Rider HTTP client.
### Start the demo first:  dotnet run --project src/Rbac.Demo -- --environment Development --urls http://localhost:5105
### Everything below is DEMO ONLY: the dev token endpoint hands out tokens without credentials.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5105

###############################################################################
### Health
###############################################################################

### Liveness: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live

### Readiness (checks the database): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready

###############################################################################
### Tokens for one seeded user per role (tenant-a unless noted)
###############################################################################

### system-admin
# @name systemAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-system-admin" }

### internal-staff
# @name internalStaff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-internal-staff" }

### agency-admin
# @name agencyAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-agency-admin" }

### agency-staff (sees only their own bookings)
# @name agencyStaff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-agency-staff" }

### corporate-staff
# @name corporateStaff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-corporate-staff" }

### finance-officer (refund-related bookings only)
# @name financeOfficer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-finance-officer" }

### report-viewer (no booking rows at all)
# @name reportViewer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-report-viewer" }

### customer (a separate principal kind, not a staff role)
# @name customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-customer" }

### system-admin of the other tenant
# @name otherTenantAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "b-system-admin" }

### Unknown demo user: 404
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "nobody" }

###############################################################################
### Who am I
###############################################################################

### Principal and live effective permissions: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### The same endpoint, different rows per role (compare totalCount)
###############################################################################

### system-admin: every booking in tenant-a (48)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### internal-staff: internal and guest bookings, none owned by an agency or corporate account (13)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{internalStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### agency-admin: the whole agency (13)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### agency-staff: only their own bookings (4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### corporate-staff: only their own bookings (3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{corporateStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### finance-officer: refund-related statuses only (12)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{financeOfficer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### customer: their own bookings (4)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### other tenant: only tenant-b's 12 bookings
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{otherTenantAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### status filter and paging: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?status=Refunded&page=1&pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### "my bookings only" narrowing: can only reduce what the role already sees
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?mine=true
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The client channel header is never an authorization input: same 4 bookings, only echoed as channelHint
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Client-Channel: back-office

### Invalid filter: 400 problem details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?status=bogus
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### By id: one rule for lists and lookups
###############################################################################

### In scope (agency-staff owns bk-a-024): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/bk-a-024
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Out of scope (bk-a-001 belongs to system-admin): 404, not 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/bk-a-001
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Another tenant's booking: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/bk-b-001
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### Writes
###############################################################################

### Create (ownership is stamped from the caller, never from the body): 201
# @name created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Flight", "amount": 250.50 }

### Cancel it (draft, in scope, bookings.cancel): 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Cancel it again: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/{{created.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Invalid amount: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "Hotel", "amount": 0 }

###############################################################################
### Users: creation graph, founding admin, one visibility rule for lists and lookups
###############################################################################

### agency-admin (the founding admin of agency-a1) lists their own agency's users only: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### system-admin lists the tenant's users, filtered by role: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users?role=agency-admin&pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A user of the caller's own agency: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### A user outside the caller's scope (the system admin): 404, not 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-system-admin
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### The founding admin creates agency staff inside their own agency: 201
# @name newStaff
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "demo-agency-staff", "displayName": "Demo agency staff", "roleKey": "agency-staff", "agencyId": "agency-a1" }

### Token for the second admin of agency-a1 (not the founding admin)
# @name secondAgencyAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "a-agency-admin-2" }

### A second agency admin cannot create admins, only the founding admin can: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{secondAgencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "demo-agency-admin", "displayName": "Demo agency admin", "roleKey": "agency-admin", "agencyId": "agency-a1" }

### An agency admin cannot create users in another agency: 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "handle": "demo-other-agency", "displayName": "Other agency", "roleKey": "agency-staff", "agencyId": "agency-a2" }

### Change the new user's role; their tokens stop working: 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{newStaff.response.body.$.id}}/role
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "roleKey": "agency-staff", "agencyId": "agency-a1" }

### Soft delete the new user: 204 (then GET returns 404 and the handle can be used again with a new id)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/{{newStaff.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### Permissions: catalog, role defaults, per-user diff with a version precondition
###############################################################################

### The permission catalog (permissions.view): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Roles with their stored default permissions: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### One role: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/roles/agency-staff
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Read a user's permissions and the version to send as If-Match (ETag header and "version" field): 200
# @name staffPermissions
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Without If-Match: 428
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "grant": ["bookings.view-all-agency"] }

### Grant and revoke in one diff with the version just read: 200 (the user's sessions are revoked, so request a new token afterwards)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "{{staffPermissions.response.body.$.version}}"

{ "grant": ["bookings.view-all-agency"], "revoke": ["bookings.cancel"] }

### Replaying the same version is now stale: 412
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "{{staffPermissions.response.body.$.version}}"

{ "reset": ["bookings.cancel"] }

### An agency admin cannot grant what they do not hold (reports.view): 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/users/a-agency-staff-viewall/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{ "grant": ["reports.view"] }

### Replace a role's defaults for the caller's own tenant (system admin only; other tenants are untouched): 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/roles/report-viewer/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "permissions": ["reports.view"] }

### The system admin cannot add a permission they do not hold (bookings.view-all-agency): 403
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/roles/finance-officer/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "permissions": ["bookings.read", "bookings.view-all-agency"] }

###############################################################################
### Audit trail (append-only; audit.view: system admin and internal admin)
###############################################################################

### Everything that changed in the tenant, newest first: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit?pageSize=50
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Filter by target and by actor: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit?target=a-agency-staff&actor=a-agency-admin
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Not allowed to read the trail: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### Acting on behalf of another user (X-On-Behalf-Of, needs users.act-on-behalf)
###############################################################################

### The system admin acts as corporate staff: the same list as that staff member sees, not the whole tenant (3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings?pageSize=100
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-On-Behalf-Of: a-corporate-staff

### /me shows the effective user and who is acting: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-On-Behalf-Of: a-corporate-staff

### Acting as a peer or a higher role is refused: 403 (here: as themselves)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-On-Behalf-Of: a-system-admin

### A user of another tenant does not exist for the caller: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-On-Behalf-Of: b-agency-staff

### Without users.act-on-behalf the header is refused, not ignored: 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/me
Authorization: Bearer {{agencyAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-On-Behalf-Of: a-agency-staff

###############################################################################
### Administration
###############################################################################

### Role by action summary from the registry (system-admin only): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/access-matrix
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### OpenAPI document (requires a token like everything else): 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/openapi/v1.json
Authorization: Bearer {{systemAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}

###############################################################################
### Denials
###############################################################################

### No token: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings

### Missing permission (report-viewer has reports.view only): 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{reportViewer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Missing permission on a gated action (finance-officer cannot cancel): 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/bookings/bk-a-004/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{financeOfficer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### Not allowed (corporate-staff does not hold access-matrix.view): 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/access-matrix
Authorization: Bearer {{corporateStaff.response.body.$.accessToken}}
